cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  code-context-engine: a local-first MCP context engine for AI coding agents
message: If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohammad Parsa
    family-names: Karkooti
    email: 1.parsa.karkooti@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/ParsaVictor/code-context-engine
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - code-retrieval
  - code-graph
  - context-engineering
  - ai-coding-assistant
  - token-efficiency
  - rust
abstract: >-
  code-context-engine answers "which files does this task need?" from a
  per-project code graph instead of re-reading a repository every turn. It
  resolves seeds from the task as written, expands along call, import and
  configuration edges, and emits a folded evidence packet for an MCP client.
  Recall and precision are published per question against hand-written gold
  sets on third-party repositories the engine was never tuned on.
references:
  - type: software
    title: NeuroMesh
